(Bug #127: a width read cleanly, then a `.` that names no precision -
 `{n:8.2z}` - used to stay the quiet no-op `{n:8}` is, on the theory that
 a dangling `.` after a width is a different clause shape from an unknown
 specifier letter. It is not: the width half is fine, but the clause as a
 whole is still nothing the table defines, exactly like `{n:8q}` already
 refused before this fix.)

a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:8.2z}".
